    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1161">

                <pb facs="1175" n="1009" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1009"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.516/170</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Fletcher to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 80</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose text and
                    translation of a decree providing for administrative liquidation of banks,
                    issued April 6, 1917 by First Chief Carranza of the Constitutionalist Army.</p>
                <pb facs="1176" n="1010" xml:id="pg1010"/>
                <p>For the information of the Department, Article 5 of the Decree of December 14,
                    1916 which is modified by the enclosed decree is translated as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>If the report of the Board of Receivers shows that the bank cannot cover
                            its liabilities with its assets, the Secretary of the Treasury will
                            order its judicial liquidation in accordance with the Decree of
                            September 15 referred to (1916).</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The decree enclosed has not yet been published in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Diario Oficial</hi> and the text was copied from a local paper.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1161-a1.xml" xpointer="d1161-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
